{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/24515","id":3635644715,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLCAjRs7Ys4kr","html_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/24515","diff_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/24515.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/24515.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/24515","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/24515/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/24515/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/issues/24515/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/statuses/4d1b909d619f517b8f0d782eba27185868def42a","number":24515,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"LPLB: linear-programming load balancer for MoE expert parallelism","user":{"login":"feliang-git","id":188128116,"node_id":"U_kgDOCzabdA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/188128116?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git","html_url":"https://github.com/feliang-git","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/feliang-git/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds LPLB (Linear Programming Load Balancer), a new MoE expert-dispatch algorithm that solves a per-layer LP to balance token routing across redundant expert replicas. Opt-in via `--ep-dispatch-algorithm=lp`; default behavior unchanged.\n\n- New `lp` choice for `--ep-dispatch-algorithm` (complements `static`, `dynamic`, `fake`).\n- 4 JIT-compiled CUDA kernels under `python/sglang/jit_kernel/csrc/lplb/`: a single-block IPM (`ipm.cuh`) using cuBLASDx for GEMMs and a hand-written block Cholesky for POSV (no `-rdc=true` device linking required), plus three more (`lp_prep`, `lp_post`, `dispatch_probability`) that fuse 8/5/7 torch ops into single launches.\n- Math-DX is the only new dependency. Resolved via `MATHDX_HOME` env var, the `nvidia-mathdx` PyPI package, or the bundled `python/sglang/jit_kernel/lplb/resources/download-mathdx.sh`.\n- Strict failure semantics: the server raises at startup if the fused backend isn't available (no CUDA, SM < 9.0, missing Math-DX); no silent fallback to torch IPM or to dynamic dispatch.\n\n## Performance\n\nMeasured on 2× H20 nodes, DeepSeek-R1, EP=16 with DP-attention, DeepEP backend, `--max-concurrency 2048`, 4096-prompt timed runs × 3 reps each, counterbalanced order:\n\n| Dataset  | dynamic tput | lp tput | Δ% | TTFT p50 Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **GSM8K**   | 19,715 | **20,779** | **+5.40%** | -5.99% |\n| MMLU     | 22,949 | 22,825 | -0.54% | -2.58% |\n| ShareGPT | 2,114  | 2,104  | -0.48% | **-9.18%** |\n\nGSM8K is the routing-skewed workload LPLB targets. MMLU and ShareGPT are nulls on throughput (LPLB doesn't regress on uniform-routing or prefill-bound workloads). ShareGPT's TTFT p50 is -9.2% — the median-user TTFT improvement, which is the load-balance signal on long-context chat workloads. n = 3 reps; all p > 0.05, but effects are directionally consistent across all metrics on GSM8K (5/5 favor LP).\n\n## Reproducing the benchmark\n\n### 0. One-time: install Math-DX\n\n```bash\n# Either via PyPI:\npip install nvidia-mathdx\n# or via the bundled script (idempotent — safe to re-run):\nbash python/sglang/jit_kernel/lplb/resources/download-mathdx.sh\n```\n\n### 1. Launch the server (run on both nodes; `--node-rank` differs)\n\n```bash\n# Required to keep the JIT path off the legacy default CUDA stream\n# under DP-attention all-reduce.\nexport NVSHMEM_IB_GID_INDEX=3\nexport NVSHMEM_IBGDA_NIC_HANDLER=cpu\nexport NVSHMEM_BOOTSTRAP_UID_SOCK_IFNAME=bond0\n\npython3 -u -m sglang.launch_server \\\n    --model-path /path/to/DeepSeek-R1 \\\n    --tokenizer-path /path/to/DeepSeek-R1 \\\n    --trust-remote-code \\\n    --host 0.0.0.0 --port 30000 \\\n    --tp-size 16 --dp-size 16 --ep-size 16 \\\n    --enable-dp-attention \\\n    --moe-a2a-backend deepep --deepep-mode normal \\\n    --ep-num-redundant-experts 16 \\\n    --ep-dispatch-algorithm lp \\\n    --init-expert-location /path/to/expert_stats.pt \\\n    --mem-fraction-static 0.8 \\\n    --max-running-requests 1024 \\\n    --max-prefill-tokens 65536 \\\n    --chunked-prefill-size 65536 \\\n    --schedule-conservativeness 0.3 \\\n    --disable-radix-cache \\\n    --nnodes 2 --node-rank 0 \\\n    --dist-init-addr <head-node-ip>:29500\n```\n\n`expert_stats.pt` is a per-dataset routing-statistics file produced by a 1000-prompt run with `--ep-dispatch-algorithm=dynamic --expert-distribution-recorder-mode=stat` and dumped via `/dump_expert_distribution_record`. The file must exist on every node (the cluster /raid is non-shared in our setup).\n\n### 2. Run the benchmark\n\n```bash\npython3 -m sglang.bench_serving \\\n    --backend sglang-oai \\\n    --base-url http://localhost:30000 \\\n    --dataset-name custom \\\n    --dataset-path /path/to/dataset.jsonl \\\n    --num-prompts 4096 \\\n    --max-concurrency 2048 \\\n    --sharegpt-output-len 4 \\\n    --output-file lp.json\n```\n\nRe-run with `--ep-dispatch-algorithm=dynamic` for the baseline. We counterbalanced 3 reps × 2 algorithms with kill-and-relaunch between every rep to control for JIT-cache and NIC-heat drift.\n\n## Scope\n\n**DeepSeek-v2 only.** Other MoE forward paths (Qwen3, GLM4, SDAR-MoE, …) return `empty_topk_output` directly without participating in the EP all-reduce; with LP active they would deadlock under DP-attention. Out of scope for this PR; future work to enable.\n\nLP additionally requires:\n- `--enable-dp-attention`\n- `--moe-a2a-backend=deepep`\n- Hopper-class GPU (SM ≥ 9.0)\n- Math-DX cuBLASDx headers reachable\n\n`check_lplb_server_args` validates the first two at startup with clear errors. The model-arch check fires at `LPLBSolver.__init__`.\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Default behavior (no LP flags) is byte-identical to pre-PR upstream — LP code paths are inert imports.\n- This PR also includes a small worker-node startup fix in `entrypoints/http_server.py` and `entrypoints/openai/serving_{base,chat}.py` (guard against `tokenizer_manager is None` for `node_rank >= 1` in multi-node serving). Happy to split into a separate PR if preferred — it's unrelated to LPLB but came up during multi-node bring-up.\n- `download-mathdx.sh` is idempotent (skips if `mathdx/include` and `mathdx/lib` are present).\n- No NCCL or NVSHMEM changes; LP runs over existing all-reduce primitives.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] Multi-rank smoke test on 2× H20 with DeepSeek-R1: server boots, `/server_info` reports `ep_dispatch_algorithm=lp`, single + 8-parallel completions return valid text.\n- [x] End-to-end 3-dataset benchmark sweep (3 datasets × 6 reps each, 18 timed runs): no errors, numbers match the table above.\n- [x] Codex review + rescue passes against the diff (P0 clean; P1 findings addressed in the last two commits).\n- [ ] CI: `pytest test/registered/eplb/test_lplb_distributed.py` under `torchrun --nproc-per-node 2` (to be triggered in CI).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\